{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Python comparison — ROML model-build benchmark{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<h1>ROML Python vs PuLP / Pyomo / PyOptInterface</h1>
<div class="notice">
<strong>Semantic boundary.</strong> PyOptInterface population calls insert
directly into a solver-backed HiGHS model, while ROML, PuLP, and Pyomo build
a separate modeling representation first. These curves compare elapsed
user-facing construction-API time under each library's documented efficient
public path — not identical internal work. Each library consumed the same
deterministic canonical input generated once per run outside the timer.
</div>
{% for title, div in charts %}
<div class="chart"><h2>{{ title }}</h2>{{ div | safe }}</div>
{% endfor %}
<h2>Construction paths</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>ROML Python (bulk)</strong> — {{ impl_notes['roml_python_bulk'] }}</li>
<li><strong>PuLP</strong> — {{ impl_notes['pulp_python'] }}</li>
<li><strong>Pyomo</strong> — {{ impl_notes['pyomo_python'] }}</li>
<li><strong>PyOptInterface</strong> — {{ impl_notes['pyoptinterface_python'] }}</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}
